    "text": "The radius through a circle's point of contact is perpendicular to the tangent there. Proof: Let XY touch a circle with centre O at P. Any other point Q on XY lies outside the circle, so OQ is longer than radius OP. Thus OP is the shortest distance from O to line XY and is perpendicular to XY.",
