    "id": "ncert.maths.ch10.p006.equal_tangents_proof",
    "text": "Tangents drawn from the same external point to a circle have equal lengths. If PQ and PR touch a circle with centre O at Q and R, join OP, OQ and OR. The radii OQ and OR are perpendicular to their tangents. Right triangles OQP and ORP have equal radii OQ = OR and common hypotenuse OP, so they are congruent by RHS. Therefore PQ = PR.",
